  "user_request_original": "Optimize a 22-layer TiO2/SiO2 dielectric stack on fused silica substrate at 45 degrees incidence. Layer sequence: TiO2|SiO2 alternating, starting with TiO2 adjacent to substrate, terminating with SiO2. Initialize all thicknesses at 120nm with random perturbations bounded to ±25% (90-150nm range). Apply soft penalty on absolute thickness difference between adjacent layers during gradient-based optimization. Wavelength bands: 450-650nm (target high reflectance), 700-1000nm (target high transmittance). Optimize all 22 thicknesses with bounds 30-250nm. Report best_target_score, valid_candidates count, tightest_margin, and thicknesses_nm for all candidates. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 450-650 nm, 700-1000 nm. soft objectives: high reflectance in 450-650 nm; high transmittance in 700-1000 nm; minimized crosstalk between bands. behaviors to suppress or avoid: transmittance in 450-650 nm; reflectance in 700-1000 nm. manufacturing constraints: maximum 24 layers.",
  "normalized_request_english": "Optimize 22 alternating TiO2/SiO2 layers on fused silica at 45° incidence. Layers alternate TiO2/SiO2 starting from air-facing side, ending with SiO2. Bounds: 30–250 nm, initialized near 120 nm. Maximize mean reflectance in 450–650 nm and maximize mean transmittance in 700–1000 nm. Apply ±25% relative thickness tolerance for robustness scoring.",
